# A line continued at the statement's own margin after a `.`, which the
# lexer reads as one statement (no terminator after the `.`, no indent at
# the same column) and design.md §4.15 defers (*trailing-operator
# continuation at depth zero*, panel 007). There are no parentheses of the
# author's to keep, and `fmt` prints its own, as it already did for a
# comment after an operator there; the trunk refused at exit 2. With the
# comment on a line of its own inside the continuation, `fmt` still refuses
# at exit 2, since the owner rule reads the continued line as a new logical
# line and the comment as a block's; that shape is reported apart.

function main()
    xs = [1, 2, 3]
    c = xs.  # at the statement's own margin, no parentheses
    len()
    print(c)
